Research decision memo — Stage 5
Title: Bouchaud-Inspired Firm Fragility with Optimal Firms
Status: NOT STARTED

Central hypothesis: Can financial fragility, defaults and employment cascades from Bouchaud-inspired macro ABMs be reconstructed with optimizing firms and clearing credit, goods and labor markets?

Feasibility prior:
Conditional: Mark-0-style heuristic behavioral rules are not automatically optimizing general equilibrium; compare the original heuristic benchmark to a separately microfounded firm model.

Core economic distinction:
Stage 0/4 equilibrium without frictions; original Bouchaud-style heuristic ABM as a labeled non-equilibrium comparator

Conditions to check:
1. Firm dynamic optimization and default/limited-liability constraints
2. Intermediary budget and loan market clearing
3. Household ownership and distribution of profits/losses
4. Aggregate resource and labor market clearing

Pass / fail criterion:
Accept only an explicitly optimized firm/credit mechanism; document which original Bouchaud properties do and do not survive.

The project reports negative feasibility results when a kinetic, entropy, adaptive-trading, or heuristic-firm mechanism cannot be reconciled with optimization and equilibrium. Do not silently weaken rational expectations or drop clearing equations.

Evidence status: no derived theorems, numerical solutions or validated simulations committed yet.
